"note_claim": "The terms \"Jewish\" and \"Jew\" are synonyms for \"Israelite\".",
"label": "SUPPORTS",
"quote": "In the late Second Temple period, the dominant meaning of the word 'Jew' continued to be an ethnic one, in its parallel connotation to the 'People of Israel.'",
"reason": "The article explicitly states that the term \"Jew\" holds a \"parallel connotation to the 'People of Israel'\" and was used alongside \"Yisrael\" to refer to the same ethnic group."
